{"repositoryId":1420985437,"availability":"available","full":"GustavoGFV/PokeBattle","name":"PokeBattle","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-15T15:59:42Z","updated":"2026-10-16T02:01:40Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://pokebattle-delta.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://pokebattle-delta.vercel.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.537Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.537Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.537Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:46.537Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A fast, lightweight, browser-based Pokémon battle simulator and team builder built with modern TypeScript and Vite. Features autonomous 6-on-6 Pokémon duels, authentic 32-bit chiptune audio synthesizers, customizable trainer rosters, shiny mechanics, dynamic dodge physics, local persistence, and real-time canvas rendering."],"features":["Autonomous Tactical Duel: Two teams of 6 Pokémon battle in real-time with speed-driven orbit physics, melee dashes, knockback effects, and elemental type matchups across 18 Pokémon types.","Dynamic Dodge System: Dodge chances are calculated dynamically from each Pokémon's base Speed stat using the formula:","$$\\text{Dodge Chance} = 25\\% \\times \\left(\\frac{\\text{Pokemon Speed}}{100}\\right)$$ (e.g., 130 Speed = 32.5% dodge chance; 30 Speed = 7.5% dodge chance). Dodges trigger an italic white floating indicator with an…","Dynamic Speed & Range Calculation: Faster Pokémon close gaps quickly and maintain optimal distance based on their moveset categories (melee punches, lunges, ranged bursts, projectiles).","Entrance Sequence: Trainers walk to their marks (TRAINERARRIVALMS, 1.8 s); only then do their Pokémon spawn with a summon effect, and the match starts when the entrance ends (ENTRANCEDURATIONMS, 2.4 s)."],"source